        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b08fffdfd3234305abca96c489ce3479",
      "statement": "The parity harness is differential over emitted files rather than over code or standard output: it bootstraps two identical fixtures and compares the resulting trees file by file.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/parity-check.sh#L26-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a746c37912d0e5e45b93e3bfdde1412ff274ea215dc93b89d54dad2b78dc6267:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6b733a6120544ec3b193b7beeaa9ed79",
      "statement": "The allowlist of sanctioned differences is a regex anchored at both ends, so a path not matching it exactly is a break.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/parity-check.sh#L37-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:03785d78b494fc5fd79374375a6601001f373ee4f35f07fe5f6d3220a14f5b04:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3d2790ec36674c688d9b2afa88b5cfd7",
      "statement": "Every sanctioned divergence traces to one root cause: the port refuses to require a JavaScript runtime in the bootstrapped repository, writing shell shims that delegate to the binary instead.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/ade-core/src/harness/claude.rs#L115-L122",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e3688bc87608edb7915cd333d06e69a7044413852a219de0e30d27bb7deb137d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d50dc6b2d72c4245affc0dca345cd3fe",
      "statement": "The harness also asserts cross-version interoperability, pointing the compiled binary at the oracle-bootstrapped fixture and requiring verify, apply, verify and audit verification to succeed with only instruction drift tolerated.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/parity-check.sh#L78-L98",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3d0e17a5a3cb1aec92f50d977048c7b27740509ce7402185b0a6656a4734d6b3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e0f1514f6ce34e4a98e096e236a7ed6a",
      "statement": "The one-sided-file check cannot fail the run, because it pipes into a loop whose body runs in a subshell so its failure flag never reaches the parent scope, unlike the first loop which uses process substitution and does propagate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/parity-check.sh#L58-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:18eb8fd55dac24cdcfc5c52c7a9521a226d2ee3affa2152723f8c4038a926787:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3fc4b6dbc61d4b5586ead28eccc20301",
      "statement": "The instruction-file content assertion is dead under the script's own pipefail setting, because the diff returns non-zero whenever the files differ and that propagates through the pipeline, so the negation always selects the no-op branch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/parity-check.sh#L67-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:39b2bceb410342260280cc167e07587747e845555d5af50eb26dc5d8852cd89b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f80d8772b17849efa8955ae47b1d67af",
      "statement": "The harness exercises only bootstrap, so commands present on both sides are never compared and a large Rust-only surface including removal and the desktop tree falls outside parity entirely.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/ade/src/main.rs#L39-L110",
